04:21:38,260 --> 04:21:39,060
I'm not sure it is.

4399
04:21:39,480 --> 04:21:40,340
I have heard about it.

4400
04:21:41,060 --> 04:21:41,660
I can check it.

4401
04:21:42,020 --> 04:21:42,340
Hold on.

4402
04:21:44,280 --> 04:21:44,620
Backlocked.

4403
04:21:47,340 --> 04:21:48,180
Maybe it is.

4404
04:21:50,040 --> 04:21:52,540
You mean what remains of Edith Finch, right?

4405
04:21:53,220 --> 04:21:54,040
It is on my backlog.

4406
04:21:57,300 --> 04:22:01,200
In fact, here it is if you want to check out what is on there and what is not on there.

4407
04:22:07,080 --> 04:22:07,700
Ma was one.

4408
04:22:07,960 --> 04:22:08,280
Hey, man.

4409
04:22:08,480 --> 04:22:09,360
Good to see you.

4410
04:22:09,940 --> 04:22:10,600
Missed the stream.

4411
04:22:10,900 --> 04:22:11,700
First time chatting here.

4412
04:22:11,800 --> 04:22:12,760
Nice to hang out with you.

4413
04:22:13,120 --> 04:22:15,720
Found you through a supercut of your playthrough of Outer Wilds.

4414
04:22:15,780 --> 04:22:16,460
And then kept watching.

4415
04:22:16,620 --> 04:22:17,460
Enjoy your noise of playthrough.

4416
04:22:18,380 --> 04:22:21,880
Man, a lot of people found me through that supercut of Elis.

4417
04:22:22,060 --> 04:22:23,660
That video went kind of viral.

4418
04:22:24,260 --> 04:22:25,040
It's crazy.

4419
04:22:27,460 --> 04:22:29,280
I think it's because of the title of it.

4420
04:22:29,540 --> 04:22:30,040
He titled it...

4421
04:22:32,240 --> 04:22:34,620
Astrophysicist Explores the Outer Wilds or something.

4422
04:22:36,900 --> 04:22:43,640
And then after that, I changed the title of the first video of my playlist to Astrophysicist Plays as well.

4423
04:22:44,460 --> 04:22:45,000
And it worked.

4424
04:22:45,360 --> 04:22:45,640
It worked.

4425
04:22:48,900 --> 04:22:50,260
Those clickbait titles.

4426
04:22:51,340 --> 04:22:53,280
Well, it's not really clickbait, I guess, in this case.

4427
04:22:53,280 --> 04:22:56,080
But it just feels like it is a little bit.

4428
04:23:00,140 --> 04:23:03,680
It's always fun when you figure out something really complex just to miss something very simple.

4429
04:23:03,800 --> 04:23:05,160
Dude, that's my life.

4430
04:23:06,700 --> 04:23:07,320
I shit you not.

4431
04:23:07,440 --> 04:23:08,220
I overthink everything.

4432
04:23:09,000 --> 04:23:10,060
And miss the simple things.

4433
04:23:10,300 --> 04:23:11,820
It's the story of my life.

4434
04:23:15,090 --> 04:23:16,490
Yo, there's a new Life is Strange coming.

4435
04:23:17,630 --> 04:23:18,430
29th of October.

4436
04:23:19,410 --> 04:23:19,670
Really?

4437
04:23:20,970 --> 04:23:22,750
But wait, isn't there already a strange...

4438
04:23:23,810 --> 04:23:25,270
I was about to say, strange new life.

4439
04:23:25,950 --> 04:23:26,810
Life is Strange 2?

4440
04:23:27,070 --> 04:23:29,190
Isn't that already out?

4441
04:23:35,090 --> 04:23:36,070
With Max Caulfield.

4442
04:23:36,870 --> 04:23:38,930
Oh, lovely.

4443
04:23:45,330 --> 04:23:47,070
I'm most likely going to check that out.

4444
04:23:52,260 --> 04:23:54,780
Oh, gee, gangster demon plays applied.

4445
04:23:57,120 --> 04:24:01,600
I was thinking of making something like that as a joke once.

4446
04:24:02,180 --> 04:24:08,060
Just a really over-the-top video, you know, with an over-the-top thumbnail and just leaning into the whole thing.

4447
04:24:08,060 --> 04:24:09,300
Just for fun.

4448
04:24:24,810 --> 04:24:27,030
It's descriptive, which can help pique your interest.

4449
04:24:27,830 --> 04:24:33,790
Knowing an actual astrophysicist plays a game about space is interesting because they'll have information tidbits to share.

4450
04:24:34,250 --> 04:24:38,150
I feel like I didn't share that much from that perspective.

4451
04:24:38,450 --> 04:24:41,260
And maybe this is a weird stance to have, but like...

4452
04:24:42,290 --> 04:24:46,610
So I've been studying this stuff for like, pretty much half of my life at this point.

4453
04:24:47,930 --> 04:24:51,410
And in the beginning, it was like a big passion of mine, you know?

4454
04:24:51,410 --> 04:24:56,330
I would talk about astro-related things to everyone I could, you know?

4455
04:24:57,190 --> 04:25:00,490
But then I've been doing it so long now that it's become so much of a job.

4456
04:25:01,270 --> 04:25:05,050
Then at the end of the day, I just don't want to talk about it anymore, even though I love it a lot.

4457
04:25:06,170 --> 04:25:09,270
You know, like, I don't want to spill too much of it.

4458
04:25:11,050 --> 04:25:13,310
Like, I just want to leave work at work, you know what I mean?

4459
04:25:13,770 --> 04:25:17,270
It's not like that all the time, but for a while it was like that for me.

4460
04:25:17,830 --> 04:25:21,070
And I kind of hated that because I used to be so passionate about it.

4461
04:25:21,410 --> 04:25:25,470
I still am to an extent, but nowhere near the level when I first started.

4462
04:25:30,900 --> 04:25:34,220
I would say games are definitely a bigger passion of mine.

4463
04:25:34,300 --> 04:25:36,300
It's something that has never subsided for me.

4464
04:25:37,320 --> 04:25:38,400
My parents used to tell me...

4465
04:25:39,080 --> 04:25:43,500
Like, I played so many video games as a child, especially when World of Warcraft Classic was out, man.

4466
04:25:43,680 --> 04:25:46,680
I was sometimes skipping school to play that shit.

4467
04:25:46,940 --> 04:25:48,700
Like, I was loving it.

4468
04:25:49,880 --> 04:25:51,820
And they would think something's wrong with me.

4469
04:25:51,880 --> 04:25:54,300
I remembered my mom took me to a psychiatrist once.

4470
04:25:55,060 --> 04:25:56,340
He plays too many video games.

4471
04:25:56,420 --> 04:25:57,080
What is wrong with him?

4472
04:25:57,140 --> 04:25:58,000
And we had a whole talk.

4473
04:25:58,860 --> 04:26:01,660
And at the end, the psychiatrist was like, nah, that's pretty normal.

4474
04:26:02,360 --> 04:26:03,300
He's a young guy.

4475
04:26:03,400 --> 04:26:04,020
He's a young kid.

4476
04:26:04,900 --> 04:26:05,840
They love video games.

4477
04:26:06,160 --> 04:26:08,120
I wouldn't think too much about it, you know?

4478
04:26:08,780 --> 04:26:11,640
And then she would tell me after that, well, one day you're going to grow out of it.

4479
04:26:11,700 --> 04:26:12,280
It's just a phase.

4480
04:26:12,540 --> 04:26:16,040
Later on, you're not going to play as many video games, you know?

4481
04:26:17,340 --> 04:26:18,400
She couldn't be more wrong.

4482
04:26:19,600 --> 04:26:22,100
I play more video games now than I've ever done.

4483
04:26:24,920 --> 04:26:25,560
I love it.

4484
04:26:26,100 --> 04:26:27,040
It's the best thing.

4485
04:26:27,660 --> 04:26:29,840
It's an escape from everything.

4486
04:26:30,380 --> 04:26:31,820
Not that I hate everything, but...

4487
04:26:33,300 --> 04:26:34,860
I just like it more, I guess.

4488
04:26:35,760 --> 04:26:36,700
It was in the face, mom.

4489
04:26:37,400 --> 04:26:37,740
Exactly.

4490
04:26:42,450 --> 04:26:45,990
I'm not sure if video gaming is hip nowadays to moms and dads.

4491
04:26:47,690 --> 04:26:48,370
And their children.

4492
04:26:48,650 --> 04:26:49,130
I don't know.

4493
04:26:49,530 --> 04:26:49,890
Maybe it is.

4494
04:26:50,690 --> 04:26:54,550
I feel like most would restrict the time on the computer, even today.

4495
04:26:59,010 --> 04:27:00,350
Do you ever get a dizzy...

4496
04:27:00,730 --> 04:27:02,910
Do you ever get dizzy watching the night sky?

4497
04:27:03,450 --> 04:27:06,930
I have a love-hate relationship with it because it feels too vast and it's overwhelming.

4498
04:27:08,750 --> 04:27:10,150
No, I think it's awesome.

4499
04:27:10,330 --> 04:27:10,830
I love...

4500
04:27:10,830 --> 04:27:12,070
I love looking at the night sky.

4501
04:27:12,210 --> 04:27:16,770
One of the best things is to lie down on the grass.

4502
04:27:17,410 --> 04:27:24,610
Like, almost like a snow angel position, you know, where you feel with your hands the grass and your feet are, like, stretched out.

4503
04:27:25,350 --> 04:27:29,930
And then you try to imagine that you're, like, holding on to the earth as it spins, you know?

4504
04:27:29,930 --> 04:27:35,430
So, you know how when something spins, centrifugal force, everything gets spun out?

4505
04:27:36,050 --> 04:27:37,190
You're trying to resist that, you know?

4506
04:27:37,230 --> 04:27:43,030
You hold on to the grass and you look up at the sky and you just try to feel the rotation of the earth.

4507
04:27:44,110 --> 04:27:46,730
When you look up at the sky, there's just something magical about it.

4508
04:27:47,590 --> 04:27:49,070
That's one of the coolest things ever.

4509
04:27:50,050 --> 04:27:50,950
You should try it.

4510
04:27:55,490 --> 04:28:00,870
There's something comforting for me, looking at the night sky.

4511
04:28:02,010 --> 04:28:07,650
Knowing that we're nothing, that whatever happens here on earth doesn't matter at all in the grand scheme of things.

4512
04:28:08,330 --> 04:28:10,750
At least to me, that's a very calming thing.

4513
04:28:13,290 --> 04:28:16,770
I know some people get anxiety from that, and that's totally legit as well.

4514
04:28:20,690 --> 04:28:22,570
Oh, God, when I do this, I feel truly insane.

4515
04:28:23,030 --> 04:28:24,810
Let me tell you what makes me insane, Sino Christ.

4516
04:28:25,850 --> 04:28:27,550
This is going to be so hard to describe, but...

4517
04:28:29,530 --> 04:28:33,070
if you... if you try to imagine not...

4518
04:28:33,510 --> 04:28:35,770
Okay, this is going to get a little ridiculous, maybe.

4519
04:28:36,530 --> 04:28:40,490
But if you try to imagine never being born, like, try to imagine not existing.

4520
04:28:42,390 --> 04:28:43,910
What did it feel like before you were here?

4521
04:28:44,490 --> 04:28:46,170
That feeling scares me so much.

4522
04:28:46,290 --> 04:28:47,790
This feeling of not being here.

4523
04:28:50,190 --> 04:28:50,950
You know what I mean?

4524
04:28:51,550 --> 04:28:56,670
Just right now, I get this existential, like, almost black hole in my heart when I think about it.

4525
04:28:56,670 --> 04:28:57,790
It's like I can feel it.

4526
04:29:00,740 --> 04:29:06,300
Maybe I don't communicate it very well right now, but just trying to imagine nothingness for me, that's the crazy thing.

4527
04:29:07,260 --> 04:29:09,160
The not having a consciousness or existing.

4528
04:29:09,900 --> 04:29:11,860
Man, that fucks me up.

4529
04:29:25,660 --> 04:29:28,960
I like how this chat went all existential and philosophical.

4530
04:29:33,270 --> 04:29:35,310
With COVID-19, gaming became more popular.

4531
04:29:36,190 --> 04:29:36,410
Yeah!

4532
04:29:37,930 --> 04:29:38,750
That's awesome.

4533
04:29:39,890 --> 04:29:43,350
More people need to be enlightened by the beauty that is gaming.

4534
04:29:47,020 --> 04:29:48,040
I play games with my kids.

4535
04:29:48,580 --> 04:29:51,360
I found a big community of parents that, dude, that's awesome, Raven Warrior.

4536
04:29:53,240 --> 04:29:56,200
I would have loved if my parents played video games with me as a child.

4537
04:29:56,500 --> 04:30:00,660
They did very rarely, but that sounds super sick, man.

4538
04:30:04,330 --> 04:30:04,930
That's cool.

4539
04:30:13,110 --> 04:30:14,670
Hop on the existential crisis train.

4540
04:30:21,660 --> 04:30:22,360
What the hell?

4541
04:30:22,360 --> 04:30:25,620
Reminds me of trying to imagine how it would be to be blind.

4542
04:30:26,440 --> 04:30:28,280
Because it's not black, it's just nothing.

4543
04:30:29,480 --> 04:30:32,120
Apparently, if you try seeing out of your needs like the same thing...

4544
04:30:33,160 --> 04:30:33,460
Wait, what?

4545
04:30:35,360 --> 04:30:36,620
I'm trying to imagine it now.

4546
04:30:36,900 --> 04:30:38,360
I instinctively closed my eyes.

4547
04:30:39,140 --> 04:30:40,440
I can't imagine that.

4548
04:30:42,120 --> 04:30:46,260
Another thing that really blows me out of the water is trying to imagine more than three dimensions.

4549
04:30:47,160 --> 04:30:48,380
You know how flat land?

4550
04:30:49,300 --> 04:30:51,840
You imagine that everything is in two dimensions, right?

4551
04:30:51,840 --> 04:31:03,980
And when a three-dimensional being comes into contact with it, like, say, a sphere, it starts off as this point, right, that spreads out to become a circle with a maximum radius, and then it decreases again until it becomes a point again.

4552
04:31:05,200 --> 04:31:08,460
Try to imagine some four-dimensional thing moving through our dimension.

4553
04:31:09,440 --> 04:31:10,820
That breaks my brain.

4554
04:31:12,360 --> 04:31:14,420
And that's honestly a little scary.

4555
04:31:15,360 --> 04:31:19,760
Trying to imagine multiple dimensions or, like, more than three dimensions.

4556
04:31:19,760 --> 04:31:20,460
Because

4557
04:31:26,020 --> 04:31:28,900
you can't see anything out of your knee, right?

4558
04:31:29,240 --> 04:31:31,040
That's how it is for blind people, just in the eyes.

4559
04:31:31,260 --> 04:31:31,860
I see what you mean.

4560
04:31:32,780 --> 04:31:35,420
Like, when you close your eyes, you are seeing something, right?

4561
04:31:36,100 --> 04:31:36,920
You're seeing darkness.

4562
04:31:39,060 --> 04:31:42,480
Whereas if you're really blind, you don't even get that sensation.

4563
04:31:42,820 --> 04:31:43,960
Or maybe you do, I don't know.

4564
04:31:45,800 --> 04:31:46,540
I've never been blind.

4565
04:31:47,000 --> 04:31:49,560
Well, I'm blind quite often, but in a different way.

4566
04:32:02,290 --> 04:32:06,470
You can almost imagine the fourth dimension, but just as I see it, it's gone.

4567
04:32:06,850 --> 04:32:07,390
You know what's funny?

4568
04:32:08,510 --> 04:32:18,770
There is a very old, but very renowned, lecturer at the University of Copenhagen who would teach quantum mechanics and string theory and all that stuff.

4569
04:32:19,030 --> 04:32:19,850
His name was Holger Pick.

4570
04:32:20,730 --> 04:32:23,110
And he was a really funny old man, you know?

4571
04:32:23,210 --> 04:32:25,210
He would wear this bicycle helmet everywhere he went.

4572
04:32:25,750 --> 04:32:26,830
And he had this funny voice.

4573
04:32:27,030 --> 04:32:27,990
He would be like, Yes!

4574
04:32:28,310 --> 04:32:30,930
And then in four dimensions, he would talk like that, right?

4575
04:32:31,610 --> 04:32:34,770
And at some point during his lectures, he is so deep in thought.

4576
04:32:35,730 --> 04:32:40,910
He would just say random shit like, Okay, so imagine you're in, like, imagine 40 dimensions.

4577
04:32:41,190 --> 04:32:42,210
Just imagine that right now.

4578
04:32:42,290 --> 04:32:44,450
And you could see in his mind, he was imagining it.

4579
04:32:45,410 --> 04:32:47,310
You know, that guy was on another level.

4580
04:32:48,050 --> 04:32:50,490
And we're just sitting there like, I'm sorry, we can't imagine that.

4581
04:32:50,670 --> 04:32:51,730
But okay, keep going.

4582
04:32:56,060 --> 04:32:57,080
Good times, man.

4583
04:32:57,960 --> 04:32:59,000
He's not teaching anymore.

4584
04:32:59,220 --> 04:33:02,860
So he retired some time ago, but he still hangs around the university quite often.

4585
04:33:03,340 --> 04:33:04,440
Because it's his life, you know?

4586
04:33:04,620 --> 04:33:06,000
He still gives talks.

4587
04:33:06,620 --> 04:33:09,000
He still talks to students, but he doesn't get paid.

4588
04:33:09,140 --> 04:33:09,660
He's just there.

4589
04:33:10,660 --> 04:33:11,520
It's freaking awesome.

4590
04:33:23,250 --> 04:33:24,990
You love thinking about four dimensional geometry.

4591
04:33:26,530 --> 04:33:27,590
Oh, man, it is exciting.

4592
04:33:27,910 --> 04:33:30,170
I love watching YouTube videos that delve into those topics.

4593
04:33:32,250 --> 04:33:38,770
Because no matter what, you can't really show four dimensions, no matter how hard you try, right?

4594
04:33:38,890 --> 04:33:41,870
Because we're limited here in this three dimensional world.

4595
04:33:42,550 --> 04:33:43,510
Man, this is getting too crazy.

4596
04:33:43,510 --> 04:33:44,750
What is this even noise anymore?

4597
04:33:47,570 --> 04:33:50,730
Okay, so I have like 20 minutes, 25 minutes until the store closes.

4598
04:33:51,310 --> 04:33:58,150
I will have to go get some sustenance, because I have a date with someone else to watch some Starcraft tournament tonight.

4599
04:33:58,770 --> 04:34:03,450
The biggest Starcraft two tournament that has ever been is happening right now.

4600
04:34:04,010 --> 04:34:05,730
And I'm freaking excited about it.

4601
04:34:05,790 --> 04:34:06,550
I need to watch it.

4602
04:34:07,430 --> 04:34:09,410
So thank you, everybody, for joining.

4603
04:34:09,750 --> 04:34:11,590
It's been an absolute pleasure again.

4604
04:34:12,750 --> 04:34:13,850
And I'll see you next time.

4605
04:34:13,990 --> 04:34:15,830
And thanks for subscribing to those that did and following.

4606
04:34:16,290 --> 04:34:17,390
I really appreciate it.

4607
04:34:18,050 --> 04:34:20,290
If you haven't checked it out yet, check out the YouTube channel.

4608
04:34:20,550 --> 04:34:22,050
I will rate another streamer right now.

4609
04:34:22,150 --> 04:34:22,610
So stay around.
